questions.solution:
Given, resistance of galvanometer $\left(\mathrm{R}_{\mathrm{g}}\right)=50 \Omega$
Number of divisions $=25 \mathrm{I}_{\mathrm{g}}=4 \times 10^{-4} \times 25=10^{-2} \mathrm{ A} 

R is the resistance connected in series of galvanometer to convert into voltmeter
 \begin{aligned}
\therefore V & =I_g\left(R_g+R\right) \\
25 & =10^{-2}(50+R) \\
\Rightarrow R & =\frac{25}{10^{-2}}-50=2500-50 \Rightarrow R=2450 \Omega \text{ in }
\end{aligned}$
series.

